div class=3D"gamut-1impzrw-FlexBox e1tc6bzh0"><div class=3D"gamut-1ag67m1-F=
lexBox e1tc6bzh0"><h1 class=3D"gamut-oqq5yh-StyledText e8i0p5k0">Command Li=
ne Interface Setup</h1><p class=3D"gamut-1dzl6xd-StyledText e8i0p5k0"><span=
 data-testid=3D"markdown" class=3D"styles_markdown__Y5HHD gamut-1leh7be-Mar=
kdownWrapper-spacingNone e1mjarmv0" spacing=3D"none">Navigate your operatin=
g system like a professional programmer</span></p><div class=3D"gamut-b63km=
8-Box e164dx5n1"><div data-testid=3D"markdown" class=3D"styles_markdown__Y5=
HHD styles_darkTheme__sfPfQ e164dx5n0 gamut-1mhtesm-MarkdownWrapper-markdow=
nStyle-spacingLoose e1mjarmv0" spacing=3D"loose"><h2 id=3D"heading-setting-=
up-your-command-line" class=3D"g-md-h2">Setting Up Your Command Line</h2>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">The command line is a powerful tool used by developers =
to find, create, and manipulate files and folders. This short tutorial will=
 walk you through the steps for setting up the command line application on =
your computer.</p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Command Line Interfaces (CLIs) come in many forms. The =
CLI we=E2=80=99ll use is called Bash</p>
<h2 id=3D"heading-what-is-bash" class=3D"g-md-h2">What is Bash?</h2>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Bash, or the __B__ourne-__A__gain __SH__ell, is a CLI t=
hat was created in 1989 by Brian Fox as a free software replacement for the=
 Bourne Shell. A shell is a specific kind of CLI. Bash is <a target=3D"_bla=
nk" href=3D"https://www.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/article/what-is-open-source" class=
=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0">=E2=80=9Copen source=E2=80=
=9D</a>, meaning anyone can read the code and suggest changes. Since its be=
ginning, it has been supported by a large community of engineers who have w=
orked to make it an incredible tool. Bash is the default shell for Linux an=
d Mac up through macOS 10.14 (Mojave). For these reasons, Bash is the most =
used and widely distributed shell. If you want to learn more about Bash, <a=
 target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bash_(Unix_shell)"=
 class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0" rel=3D"noopener">this =
Wikipedia article</a> is a good place to start. Better yet, try it yourself=
 with one of our <a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://www.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/ca=
talog/language/bash" class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0">Ba=
sh courses</a>.</p>
<h2 id=3D"heading-bash-setup-for-mac-and-windows" class=3D"g-md-h2">Bash Se=
tup for Mac and Windows</h2>
<h3 id=3D"heading-mac-users" class=3D"g-md-h3">Mac users:</h3>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">As mentioned before, Bash is the default shell on Linux=
 and MacOS up through version 10.14 (Mojave), so good news, you don=E2=80=
=99t have to install anything! MacOS version 10.15 (Catalina) and higher us=
es a similar, but slightly different default shell called Z shell or Zsh. I=
n most ways Zsh is an exact replacement for Bash, so there is no need to sw=
itch over or install Bash instead.</p>
<div class=3D"g-md-iframe gamut-1ibjdhi-Box ebnwbv90"><div class=3D"gamut-g=
xcypp-ReactVideoPlayer e179321e1" style=3D"width: 100%; height: 100%;"><div=
 style=3D"width: 100%; height: 100%;"><iframe frameborder=3D"0" allowfullsc=
reen=3D"" allow=3D"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-medi=
a; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy=3D"strict-origi=
n-when-cross-origin" title=3D"Lesson Supplement How to setup the command li=
ne terminal Mac OS" width=3D"100%" height=3D"100%" src=3D"cid:frame-7AC7D4C=
19F1A55749D6946767D17D81F@mhtml.blink" id=3D"widget2" data-gtm-yt-inspected=
-218=3D"true"></iframe></div></div></div>

<p class=3D"g-md-p">To access Bash in MacOS, you can use an application cal=
led <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">Terminal</strong>.</p>
<ol class=3D"g-md-ol">
<li class=3D"g-md-li"><p class=3D"g-md-p">First open the <strong class=3D"g=
-md-strong">Applications</strong> folder, then open the <strong class=3D"g-=
md-strong">Utilities</strong> folder.</p>
</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li"><p class=3D"g-md-p">Once you=E2=80=99re in the <stron=
g class=3D"g-md-strong">Utilities folder</strong> you will see the applicat=
ion <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">Terminal</strong>. Open the <strong class=
=3D"g-md-strong">Terminal</strong> application and you=E2=80=99re ready to =
go!</p>
</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li"><p class=3D"g-md-p">For ease of access later, you can=
 keep Terminal in your Dock. Simply right click (alt-click) the Terminal ic=
on in your dock, then select =E2=80=9COptions=E2=80=9D, then =E2=80=9CKeep =
In Dock.=E2=80=9D</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Continue to the =E2=80=9CTry it Out!=E2=80=9D section b=
elow for some simple first steps with your new tool.</p>
<h3 id=3D"heading-windows-users" class=3D"g-md-h3">Windows users:</h3>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Windows has a different CLI, <strong class=3D"g-md-stro=
ng">Command Prompt</strong>. While this has many of the same features as Ba=
sh, Bash is much more popular. Because of the strength of the open source c=
ommunity and the tools it provides, mastering Bash is a better investment t=
han mastering the Command Prompt.</p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">To use Bash on a Windows computer, we will download and=
 install a program called <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">Git Bash</strong>. =
Git Bash allows us to easily access Bash as well as another tool we=E2=80=
=99ll be using later called Git, inside the Windows environment. (If you ha=
ven=E2=80=99t used Git before, try out <a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https:/=
/www.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/learn/learn-git" class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBa=
se e14vpv2g0">Learn Git &amp; GitHub course</a>.)</p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">You can either watch the following video, or read the r=
est of this article.</p>
<div class=3D"g-md-iframe gamut-1ibjdhi-Box ebnwbv90"><div class=3D"gamut-g=
xcypp-ReactVideoPlayer e179321e1" style=3D"width: 100%; height: 100%;"><div=
 style=3D"width: 100%; height: 100%;"><iframe frameborder=3D"0" allowfullsc=
reen=3D"" allow=3D"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-medi=
a; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy=3D"strict-origi=
n-when-cross-origin" title=3D"Lesson Supplement How to Setup the Command Li=
ne Using Git Bash on Windows OS" width=3D"100%" height=3D"100%" src=3D"cid:=
frame-E7E631929EE9E7C38B52A3A4E242B957@mhtml.blink" id=3D"widget4" data-gtm=
-yt-inspected-218=3D"true"></iframe></div></div></div>


<h4 id=3D"heading-how-to-install-git-bash" class=3D"g-md-h4">How to install=
 Git Bash:</h4>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">1. Navigate to the <a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https:/=
/git-for-windows.github.io/" class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vp=
v2g0" rel=3D"noopener">Git Bash installation page</a> and click the Downloa=
d button.=20
<img alt=3D"download" class=3D"g-md-img" src=3D"https://content.AI Academy by RiWoT.=
com/courses/freelance-1/unit-3/git%20bash%20setup/annotated_gitbash_dl.png"=
>
2. Once Git Bash is downloaded, run the downloaded <strong class=3D"g-md-st=
rong">.exe</strong> file and allow the application to make changes to your =
PC. You will get a prompt that says =E2=80=9CDo you want to allow this app =
to make changes to your device?=E2=80=9D Click <strong class=3D"g-md-strong=
">Yes</strong>.
<br class=3D"g-md-br"> <br class=3D"g-md-br">
3. To keep things simple, we will use the default settings for everything i=
n this installation, so all you need to do now is keep clicking <strong cla=
ss=3D"g-md-strong">Next</strong>, and finally <strong class=3D"g-md-strong"=
>Finish</strong>.
<img alt=3D"setup" class=3D"g-md-img" src=3D"https://content.AI Academy by RiWoT.com=
/courses/freelance-1/unit-3/git%20bash%20setup/annotated_gitbash_installer.=
png">
4. Open the Start menu by clicking on the Windows icon and typing =E2=80=9C=
Git Bash=E2=80=9D into the search bar.  The icon for Git Bash and the words=
 =E2=80=9CGit Bash Desktop App=E2=80=9D will appear. Click on the icon or t=
he words =E2=80=9CGit Bash Desktop App=E2=80=9D to open Git Bash.
<img alt=3D"openGitBash" class=3D"g-md-img" src=3D"https://content.codecade=
my.com/courses/freelance-1/unit-3/git%20bash%20setup/annotated_gitbash_star=
t.png">
5. A new window will open. This is the Git Bash CLI where we will run Bash =
commands. Whenever a new window of the Git Bash app is opened, you will alw=
ays be placed in the same directory, your <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">hom=
e directory</strong>. </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">The home directory is represented by the tilde sign, <c=
ode class=3D"g-md-code">~</code>, in the CLI after <code class=3D"g-md-code=
">MINGW64</code>. The tilde is another way to say <code class=3D"g-md-code"=
>/c/Users/username</code> in Git Bash or  <code class=3D"g-md-code">C:\home=
\Users\username</code> in Windows=E2=80=99 Command Prompt. </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">The absolute path of your current working directory, ho=
w you got from the root directory to the directory you are currently in, wi=
ll always be noted at the top of the window:</p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"homeDirectory" class=3D"g-md-img" src=3D"ht=
tps://content.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/courses/freelance-1/unit-3/git%20bash%20setup/=
annotated_gitbash_shell_edited.png"></p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Git Bash works by giving you a CLI that acts like a Bas=
h CLI. That means you can now work with your files and folders using Bash c=
ommands instead of Windows commands.</p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Congratulations, you now have Bash installed on your co=
mputer, ready to use!
In case you wanted to try out the built-in Windows command line for basic s=
ystem tasks, we talk about it in <a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://www.c=
odecademy.com/courses/learn-the-command-line/articles/windows-command-line"=
 class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0">this article</a>.</p>
<h2 id=3D"heading-try-it-out" class=3D"g-md-h2">Try it out!</h2>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Now that you have your Command Line Interface open on y=
our desktop, you are ready to use it. Go ahead and try some of the commands=
 on your personal computer. Here are some good commands for practice:</p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">1. <code class=3D"g-md-code">ls</code> to list the cont=
ents of the current directory. It may look something like this:</p>
<pre class=3D"g-md-pre"><pre class=3D"gamut-mu6hz5 e1rzuoz70"><code><div da=
ta-lang=3D"shell" class=3D"gamut-1rlug0v epnovk10"><span><span class=3D"mtk=
1">$ </span><span class=3D"mtk4">ls</span></span><br><span><span class=3D"m=
tk1">Applications&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbs=
p;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pictures</span></span><br><span><span=
 class=3D"mtk1">AI Academy by RiWoT&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Public</span></span><br><spa=
n><span class=3D"mtk1">Desktop&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nb=
sp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;=
&nbsp;Downloads</span></span><br><span><span class=3D"mtk1">Documents&nbsp;=
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nb=
sp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Library</span></span><br><span><span></spa=
n></span><br></div></code></pre></pre>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">2. <code class=3D"g-md-code">mkdir test</code> to make =
a new directory named <code class=3D"g-md-code">test</code>. Now, when you =
type <code class=3D"g-md-code">ls</code> you should see a folder called <co=
de class=3D"g-md-code">test</code>:</p>
<pre class=3D"g-md-pre"><pre class=3D"gamut-mu6hz5 e1rzuoz70"><code><div da=
ta-lang=3D"shell" class=3D"gamut-1rlug0v epnovk10"><span><span class=3D"mtk=
1">$ </span><span class=3D"mtk4">ls</span></span><br><span><span class=3D"m=
tk1">Applications&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbs=
p;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pictures</span></span><br><span><span=
