nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Public</span></span><br><spa=
n><span class=3D"mtk1">Desktop&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nb=
sp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;=
&nbsp;Downloads</span></span><br><span><span class=3D"mtk1">Documents&nbsp;=
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nb=
sp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Library</span></span><br><span><span class=
=3D"mtk1">test</span></span><br><span><span></span></span><br></div></code>=
</pre></pre>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">3. <code class=3D"g-md-code">cd test</code> to navigate=
 into the new directory. You won=E2=80=99t see an output when you do this.<=
/p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">4. <code class=3D"g-md-code">echo "Hello Command Line" =
&gt;&gt; hello_cli.txt</code> to create a new file named <code class=3D"g-m=
d-code">hello_cli.txt</code> and add <code class=3D"g-md-code">Hello Comman=
d Line</code> to that file. When you type <code class=3D"g-md-code">ls</cod=
e>, you should see the following:</p>
<pre class=3D"g-md-pre"><pre class=3D"gamut-mu6hz5 e1rzuoz70"><code><div da=
